# O3 done: ProtocolStore on the durable event log

Branch: `khamis1992/om-o3` (worktree `C:\Users\khamis\orca\workspaces\manus-local\om-o3`)
Commit: `b328694` "O3: ProtocolStore on event log"
Base branch: `manus-parity`

## What changed

### `src/protocol/store.ts` (rewritten, BUILD_SPEC §6.3)

- `appendEvent` now persists each frame through `eventLog.append()` **synchronously**
  (the row is durable before the frame is broadcast), and stamps the new
  `envelope.seq`. The in-memory `events` array is a cache only.
- `setTitle` / `setStatus` / `setTaskId` / `deleteTask` / `undeleteTask` append a
  `status` row; session metadata (task id, title, status, created/updated, soft
  delete) is folded out of those rows by a private `load()` on construction.
- **Removed** the 100 ms debounced whole-file `protocol-sessions.json` write.
- The constructor calls `migrateLegacySessions(legacySessionsFile())` (O2) in a
  try/catch before `load()`, so a legacy import failure cannot stop the adapter.
- Added `eventsAfterSeq(sessionId, afterSeqValue)` (the preferred O4 replay path).
- Every public method signature is unchanged; `ensureSession`, `getSession`,
  `getSessionByTaskId`, `bindTask`, `listSessions`, `isDeleted`, `clear` all kept.

### `src/protocol/types.ts`

- Added the optional `seq?: number` field to `ServerEnvelope` (§6.4) so a replay
  cursor can be resolved from the log.

### `src/protocol/__tests__/storeCompat.test.ts` (new)

- Writes a legacy `protocol-sessions.json` fixture to a temp `LOAM_DATA_DIR`
  before module import, then asserts restart equivalence (sessions, titles,
  statuses, task index, soft delete), replay by cursor id and by seq, one-time
  legacy import, and that `protocol-sessions.json` is **never rewritten**
  (byte-identical after every write).

